V4 actual run built/packed954 members, SHA256
3f3ae85116f12ab4354a6103c0c95e967c4e88bd2eb133e63236148a2734af49.
Its source48+50+67+35+12=212 cases and two type groups passed. Then the runner
opened source/__consumer/n14.mjs before it existed: setupConsumer's finite copy
list omitted that already staged/authenticated harness file. N14 never launched.
Ten direct children closed, zero observed RegexWorkers, five loader reservations,
no signals. Raw v4 remains FAILED_OR_INCOMPLETE, not a completed cohort.

V5 adds ONLY n14.mjs to that fixture copy list, uses new runner/outer/output names,
and requires the actual unchanged v4 whole-package SHA after its fresh build.
No source, assertions, old artifacts or permissions change. All672 main identities
are a new versioned replay, not retrocredit. The two production builds are distinct
actual attempts, not a one-build claim. Existing45min clock is NOT reset.

V5 admission carries prior10 children/5 loader reservations into its cumulative
guard, prior2,909,943 capture bytes and56,511,477 retained scratch bytes into bounds.
Per-version direct observations remain distinguishable in the receipt.

Fresh v5 retains seven mutation/restoration roles and two binding refusals.
V4 consumed five loader admissions; planned v5 uses34, total39<=40 in this grant.
Prior ten direct children plus planned44, supervisors/admin are accounted apart
from loader reservations; no transitive/kernel census inferred. Safety failures
still stop; this is the expressly permitted captured, retired helper correction.

V4 retained roots: /tmp/strict-n14-v4-author-rD68Yv and
/tmp/strict-n14-v4-launch-dafouN. No cleanup or mutation of those roots.

